DISPATCHER lane BLOCKED: BEB-2541 — mastra tick codegen FAILED: CODEGEN_WALL patch: the model's edits do not apply to the deployed source (block 1/2 SEARCH text not found in the file, even ignoring indentation: "const m = url.pathname.match(/^/status/(.+)$/);
if (m) {
  const site = m[1];
"). The file was NOT rewritten from scratch — that is what this mode exists to prevent.. Retryable if transient (BEB-2201).

CC — BOTH SURFACES LIVE AND MEASURED. GERS answers with a key; TUI contract VERIFIED. Gaps named, not glossed.

BEB-2230 GERS API — https://orky-beb-2230.alex-rollin.workers.dev · commit 17fd0707
AUTH header is X-API-Key, not Bearer. Unauth → 401 on every route including /health, exactly as the ticket specifies.
```
GET /health              200  {"health_status":"OK"}
GET /search?q=cafe       200  {"search_results":[],"message":"No results found"}
GET /place/abc123        200  {"gers_id":"abc123","message":"Placeholder for place lookup"}
POST /resolve            200  {"resolve_candidate":{},"message":"No candidate found"}
POST /resolve/bulk       200  {"bulk_resolve_results":[],"message":"No results found"}
GET /near                404  unknown route
```
LATENCY, 5 runs of /search, verbatim: 0.211 · 0.202 · 0.266 · 0.302 · 0.187 s — p50 ≈ 0.21s. Per the ticket the first honest measurement IS the baseline.

TWO REAL GAPS: /near is not implemented at all, and /place returns a self-declared placeholder rather than a lookup. The empty results from /search and /resolve are NOT a defect — there is no data behind them until the globe mirror (BEB-2579) lands, and "No results found" over an empty store is the correct answer.

BEB-2568 TUI — https://orky-beb-2568.alex-rollin.workers.dev · contract 6805c0dc VERDICT: VERIFIED, all three elements. Renders: Settings · Bot token · Chat id · Save and test · Status: never tested. That is m13934 acceptance 7 exactly — nothing stored, form renders, state named. Acceptances 1-5 prove out when a real token goes in through the surface.

WHAT UNSTUCK THE TUI is worth keeping: the contract asserted the literal text "never tested" while the spec only named a SCREEN STATE called EMPTY. Codegen rendered the state's name and the contract refused it — correctly — forever. Neither side was wrong; the spec never said what the page must CONTAIN. Exact strings into the ticket → SPEC.md → built right on the next lap.

